1. d4 d5 2. c4 Nf6 { A common mistake among weaker players. It gives white the center. } { [%csl Gd5][%cal Gf6d5] } 3. cxd5 Nxd5 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. e4 Nf6 6. Nc3 { [%csl Bc3,Bd4,Be4,Bf3] } 6... Bg4 { [%csl Rd4][%cal Rg4f3,Rc6d4] } 7. d5 Ne5 { This looks aggressive, but it is a significant blunder. } { [%csl Bf3][%cal Be5f3,Bg4d1] } 8. Nxe5 { [%csl Rd1][%cal Rg4d1] } 8... Bxd1 9. Bb5+ { [%cal Bb5e8] } 9... c6 (9... Nd7 10. Bxd7+ Qxd7 11. Nxd7 Kxd7 12. Kxd1 { White is ahead a whole minor piece. } { [%csl Gc3] }) 10. dxc6 a6 11. c7+ { [%csl Rd8][%cal Gb5e8,Rc7d8] } 11... axb5 12. cxd8=Q+ Rxd8 13. Nxd1 { White is ahead a whole minor piece. } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Be1g1] } *


