1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. Nf3 { Instead of e4 immediately... } { [%csl Gf3][%cal Gg1f3,Re2e4] } 4... O-O 5. Bg5 { Another good system you can play against King's Indian, known as "Smyslov System" } 5... d6 6. e3 { [%csl Ge3,Gd4,Gf2][%cal Rg7d4,Gf2d4] } 6... Nbd7 7. Be2 { [%cal Ge1g1] } 7... c6 8. Qc2 { [%cal Rh7h6] } 8... Qc7 (8... h6 { [%cal Rh6g5] } 9. Bh4 g5 { [%cal Rg5h4] } 10. Bg3 Nh5 { [%csl Rg3][%cal Rh5g3] } 11. Nxg5 { [%csl Bh7][%cal Bc2h7,Bg5h7,Re2h5] } 11... hxg5 (11... Nxg3 12. Qh7#) 12. Bxh5 { [%csl Gh2] }) 9. O-O (9. h4 e5 10. O-O-O a6 11. Bd3 b5) 9... e5 { Black must attack white's strong center. } { [%cal Re5d4] } 10. Rfd1 Re8 11. Rac1 { This is the position you want to reach in this system. } { [%csl Gc2,Gc3,Gc1,Gd1,Ge2,Gf3,Gg5,Bf2,Be3,Bd4,Bc4][%cal Bf2d4,Bd4c4] } 11... Nf8 12. b4 { [%csl Gc5][%cal Bf3d2,Bd2c4,Bc4d6,Gc4c5] } *


