1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 { Budapest Gambit, a very famous opening. } { [%csl Re5] } 3. dxe5 Ng4 { [%cal Rg4e5] } 4. Bf4 { Best way to defend the pawn. } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gf4e5] } 4... Nc6 5. Nf3 Bb4+ { [%cal Rb4e1] } 6. Nbd2 { We're blocking with the knight on e2 to avoid the rupture of our pawn structure. } { [%csl Gd2,Rc3][%cal Gb1d2] } 6... Qe7 { [%csl Be5][%cal Be7e5,Bc6e5,Bg4e5] } 7. e3 Ngxe5 8. Nxe5 { Exchange one pair of knights } 8... Nxe5 9. Be2 { [%cal Ge1g1] } 9... O-O 10. O-O d6 11. Nb3 { [%csl Rc4][%cal Gd2b3] } 11... Be6 { This is a blunder- we have created a trap! } { [%csl Rc4][%cal Re6c4,Re5c4] } 12. a3 { [%csl Rb4][%cal Rb4a5] } 12... Bc5 { The d6 pawn has become overloaded. } { [%csl Rd6][%cal Rd6c5,Rd6e5] } 13. Nxc5 dxc5 14. Bxe5 { White is ahead a whole minor piece. } { [%csl Ge5] } *


