1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. f3 { White's idea here is to secure the e4 square with a pawn. This game was played with V. Anand and M. Carlsen in 2011. } { [%csl Re4][%cal Rf3e4,Re2e4] } 4... d5 { [%csl Ge4][%cal Gd5e4] } 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 c5 7. cxd5 exd5 8. e3 { [%csl Gd3][%cal Gf1d3] } 8... c4 { [%csl Rd3][%cal Rc4d3] } 9. Ne2 Nc6 10. g4 O-O 11. Bg2 Na5 { Knight is going to the very nice home on b3, as no pawns will ever be able to chase it away from that point. } { [%csl Gb3][%cal Ga5b3,Rc2c3,Ra2a3] } *


